  "title": "The diminished 7th chord",
  "summary": "Minor 3rds all the way up: the most tense chord of all.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Diminished 7th chord",
      "body": "Stack three minor 3rds and you get a **diminished 7th chord**: Bdim7 is B D F A♭. Its 7th is a half step lower than in the half-diminished chord. It is written **dim7** or **°7**.\n\n**Why it matters:** Every note is 3 half steps from the next, so it sounds suspended in mid-air. It is a classic passing chord between two others, and the spooky sound of old film scores.",
